Reminds me of one of my ideas: When you're killed by a ghost, the ghost
will take over your body, and this combination will be stored as a 
savegame of the original player of the ghost.  In order to do so, a
ghost level should keep sufficient information about the original player.
If a saved gamed for that player already existed, that one would take
precedence, or the new one could be saved under a special name.

And another one, not related: To make the game *real* hard, why not let
genocided creatures be sent to Hell, where they can make the adventurers'
life just that, a hell !


